        "department": null,
        "description": "The course is an exploration of the prevailing theories, topics and empirical methods in the study of Social Psychology. It will specifically focus on five main areas: (1) the science of Social Psychology and its theoretical foundations, (2)research methods used in Social Psychology research, (3) the individual in context to the social world, (4) an individual's impact on another individual or group/s, and (5) The dynamics of social relationships.",
